  "officialAlternative": {
    "url": "https://studiegids-archief.leidenuniv.nl/studies/10721/italiaanse-taal-en-cultuur",
    "inspection": "Read the official 2025–2026 archived prospectus, years 1–3. It lists an earlier first-year linguistics sequence, 10 EC each for second-year Italian IIa and IIb, and a different third-year arrangement of two fixed seminars, two monographic options, 30 EC open choice and a 10 EC thesis. Repeated older codes, superficially similar credits and prior offerings do not establish an approved replacement or equivalence for the 2026 entrants. The current regulatory landing and plausible programme PDF returned access-block HTML. Indexed official search surfaced the 2025–2026 programme-specific regulation and faculty rules, without an adopted current bridge."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Current and forward-year programme requests returned the same 2026–2027 payload in both languages. This confirms the annual menu rather than evidence of future cohort arrangements. BA-ITA-2-V2 is an ALL group of 20 EC; BA-ITA-3-K is a separate EQ group of 15 EC. Four identical codes and offering identifiers appear in both. Only 5603ICLCY is distinct, accounting for 5 EC. No current rule in the programme or group notes allows additional counting or lists two replacements.",
    "The catalogue shows Italian IIb targets B2 production with stronger receptive skills. Sociolinguistica is listed in semester one with a prior 5 EC subject requirement, B2–C1 spoken Italian and other language conditions. Cinema and Literature requires B2 Italian. The approved pathway cannot be inferred from those course descriptions or assumed to admit students at an earlier stage.",
    "The 10 EC thesis still names legacy Taalvaardigheid IIa through IId, in addition to passing year one and 40 EC of year two. The programme now lists two 10 EC units, Lingua italiana IIa and IIb. Matching credits and the historical guide do not document which current courses the thesis board accepts for this cohort."
  ],
